# Sofie Automation Rundown Editor (`superflytv-sofie-automation-rundown-editor`)

Sofie Rundown Editor is a web tool for creating and editing Sofie rundowns in a demo environment. It connects to a Sofie Core (release 53) instance with the demo blueprints uploaded, lets you configure the Core connection, import demo Piece Types and a demo rundown, and then sync that rundown into Sofie so you can open and work with it in the Sofie Core UI.

As an Eyevinn Open Source Cloud managed service, you can spin up Sofie Rundown Editor without packaging containers, managing ports and volumes, or handling database file placement and migrations yourself. You get an instantly provisioned instance that fits into the OSC way of running open source services, while still working the same way as the upstream project: point it at your Sofie Core address, attach it as a device in Sofie, and start importing and syncing rundowns.

[Source](https://github.com/SuperFlyTV/sofie-automation-rundown-editor)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "superflytv-sofie-automation-rundown-editor"
  name       = "myeditor"

  parameters = {
    # CoreHost = "..."
    # CorePort = "..."
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CoreHost` | string | no | Hostname of the Sofie Core the editor connects to. Applied as the initial Core address when the instance first starts, and only while the saved address is still the default 127.0.0.1; an address saved on the editor's Settings page is kept. On OSC use Core's cluster-internal host from the Core instance details; its public URL is behind the OSC auth gate. Feeds CORE_HOST. |
| `CorePort` | string | no | Port of the Sofie Core the editor connects to. Applied as the initial Core port when the instance first starts, and only while the saved port is still the default 3000; a port saved on the editor's Settings page is kept. Use the internal port listed in the Core instance details. Feeds CORE_PORT. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
